# Vertex UI guide (client only)

Everything here lives in `VertexClient/` only - none of it is mirrored to `VertexServer/`.

## The shell

`pages/MainMenu` is the one main window: a `Sidebar` (left) + `TopBar` + a `CardLayout` of pages keyed by
the constants in `pages/Pages` (`HOME`, `GAMES`, `FRIENDS`, `CHAT`, `FORUMS`, `SHOP`, `PROFILE`,
`SETTINGS`, ...). Navigation goes through `MainMenu.onNavigate(pageKey)`, which first asks a hosted game
whether leaving is OK (`games.EmbeddedGamePanel.requestLeave()`).

- **Games never open their own window.** A game is an `EmbeddedGamePanel` placed into the single game-host
  slot with `MainMenu.showGame(panel)` and removed with `returnToGames()`. Any new game follows this.
- Pressing Play first shows `games.GameDetailPanel` (the "about this game" page, `Pages.GAME_DETAIL`); its
  Back returns to whichever page opened it.
- In-match chat is `chat.MatchChatDock`, docked at the EAST side of the game host; `MainMenu` creates it
  when the server announces a room.
- Match resume after a dropped connection: `pages/MatchResume` and `pages/SessionRestorer`.

## Theming - never hardcode a colour

- Colours are **roles**, not values: `theme.ThemeColor` (`BG_APP`, `BG_PANEL`, `ACCENT`, `TEXT_PRIMARY`,
  `TEXT_MUTED`, `BORDER`, ...). Resolve with `ThemeManager.getColor(ThemeColor.X)` at paint time.
- There are ~10 themes (`theme/*Theme.java`). A component must repaint when the theme changes:
  `ThemeManager.addListener(Runnable)` (and remove it when the component goes away).
- Fonts and sizes come from `theme.UITheme` (`FONT_HEADING`, `FONT_BODY`, `FONT_SMALL`, `RADIUS_PANEL`, ...).
  Call `UITheme.applyAntialiasing(g2)` in custom painting.
- **Games keep their own fixed palettes** (`theme.GameColors`, or colours inside the game) - board colours are
  part of the game's identity and don't follow the app theme.

## Use the existing components before writing new ones

`ui/`: `RoundedPanel` (themed rounded background), `ThemedButton(text, primary)`, `ThemedLabel(text, role)`,
`ThemedTextField`, `ThemedPasswordField`, `ThemedTextArea`, `ThemedScrollBarUI`, `PageHeader(title)`,
`PlaceholderPanel.show(container, text)` (empty/loading/error state), `GameHubDialog.show(anchor, title, msg)`
(the themed replacement for `JOptionPane` messages), `SidebarButton`, `StatusPill`, `StatusDot`,
`ToggleSwitch`, `HeroBanner`, `GameModeCard`. Copy the look of a neighbouring page rather than inventing one.

## Pitfalls that have already cost time

- **HTML in a `JLabel`:** `<body style='width:...'>` is ignored on the JDKs in use, so wrapped text comes out
  clipped or one line wide. Put the width on a `<table width='...'>` instead.
- **`ThemedTextField.setEnabled(false)` does not disable the inner field.** Use `setInputEnabled(...)`.
- **Buttons truncate** ("Offer ...") when a fixed `setPreferredSize` is too narrow for the label - size for the
  longest label.
- **BorderLayout keeps replaced children:** adding to `EAST` again leaves the old component in the container -
  `remove(old)` first.
- **Never do network calls on the Swing thread.** `NetworkManager.send(...)` blocks (up to 10 s); call it from a
  background thread and hop back with `SwingUtilities.invokeLater`. `sendAsync(...)` is fire-and-forget.
- A new server response type must be listed in `NetworkManager.RESPONSE_TYPES`, otherwise it is delivered as a
  push and a blocking `send()` times out.
- An `undecorated` `JFrame` harness must end with `System.exit(0)` or the JVM hangs on the AWT thread.
- Do not put a field/param named `ui` in a class you also need `ui.X` for - it shadows the package (use an import).

## Assets

- The logo is `vertex_logo.png` (loaded by `games/GameLogo`) and `vertex_icon.ico` (the window icon, multi-size).
  Copies live at the repo root, in `VertexClient/`, `VertexServer/` and `website/static/`. Replace files at the
  same names; no Java changes are needed. A new logo must be an original design.
